{{Quote|Born of ancient dragon blood, Dracos carry incredible strength and resilience.}}
'''Draco''' is one of the three [[races]] that can be obtained through a quest, exclusively in the [[Third Sea]].

Draco offers strong boosts, excelling at supporting allies and weakening enemies by reducing their damage, speed, and skills. Its [[Race Awakening]] adds damage reflection and burst, making it great for PvP, teams, PvE, and [[sea events]]. While it lacks speed, its high output and enemy debuffs from V3 and V4 compensate well, often turning fights in the user’s favor. However, its awakening creates a large sphere surrounding the user having heavy VFX, which can cause lag to low-end devices, creating a grave disadvantage for players having such media of playing. 

==Obtainment==
To begin, the player needs to get 500+ mastery on [[Dragon Talon]] and obtain all the [[Dojo Belt]]s. Then speak with the [[Dragon Wizard]], from whom they can obtain the [[Dragon Tether]] ability in order to obtain a [[Dragon Egg]] from the [[Prehistoric Island]]. The player then needs to follow the steps below to fully upgrade Draco:

{{Race Stages Table
|V1 = Draco can be obtained by exchanging {{Dragon Egg|1}} [[Dragon Egg]] with the [[Dragon Wizard]] after acquiring the [[Dojo Belt (Black)]]. Once unlocked, the player can switch to Draco anytime without the need of trading in another [[Dragon Egg]] or any {{Fragment|Fragments}}, just like [[Ghoul]].
|V2 = To unlock the V2, the player must speak to the [[Dragon Wizard]] and collect {{Fire Flower|5}} [[Fire Flowers]], which are randomly dropped from NPCs. This has a very low chance of dropping and is very time consuming. After collecting all five, return to the [[Dragon Wizard]] with {{Money|1,000,000}} [[Money]] to complete the upgrade.
* Each flower has a 5-minute cooldown.
** The player can skip the 5 minute cooldown by server hopping.
** The flowers have a delayed spawn.
* The level requirement of this quest is 2000.
|V3 = To unlock the V3, the player must first complete the [[Horned Man|Horned Man Quest]]. After, the player will have to to talk to the [[Dragon Wizard]] and defeat a [[Terrorshark]], dealing at least 10% damage. Then return to him to buy the V3 for {{Money|3,000,000}} [[Money]].
|V4 = To unlock the V4, the player must complete the [[Draco/Race Awakening Puzzle|Draco Awakening Puzzle]].
}}

